      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned in the .yaml descriptor, you can just loop over all the `bom`. `fab`, and `board` GPIOs here.  You shouldn\u0027t use a nodelabel when the device node you\u0027re working with already has the references you need,\n\n```\n    for (int i; i \u003c FAB_GPIOs; i++) {\n        gpio_port \u003d config-\u003efab_gpios[i].port;\n        if (!device_is_ready(gpio_port)) }\n            device_init(gpio_port);\n        }\n    }\n    /* Repeat for bom and board GPIOs */\n```\n\nThe `device_is_ready()` check ensures you don\u0027t initialize the same GPIO port twice.",
