      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T23:37:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In practice, you\u0027re treating this property as a boolean because the driver is directly looking up the nodelabel of pca5xx.  This also assumes that you only need to initialize a single GPIO controller.\n\nI think there 2 viable options here:\n1. Make this property a boolean. This will require that the driver loops through all GPIO driver device handles and checks all of them to see if they are ready.\n2. Make this a `phandles` property so that you can specify multiple GPIO nodes that need deferred initialization.\n\nI think option 1 has the right balance of configurability and simplicity.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 0
      },
